# TODO - Ternary machine lowering

## Objective

Lower typed C IR into a compact ternary virtual-machine representation suited to
Malbolge instead of translating C operations directly instruction by
instruction.

## Acceptance

- Every IR operation lowers to explicit ternary/runtime operations with defined
  pre/postconditions and no direct host implementation of guest computation.
- Guest-runtime semantic identities supplied by `guest-runtime-and-allocator`,
  including fundamental byte I/O and allocation/runtime helpers, lower to
  executable ternary/Malbolge-oriented operations without host callback
  substitution.
- The stage has deterministic input/output form, rejects malformed or
  unsupported input explicitly, and preserves source/profile provenance needed
  downstream.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- All declared prerequisites are completed: `typed-compiler-ir`,
  `guest-runtime-and-allocator`, `malbolge-specific-optimization-mathematics`,
  and `documentation-readiness-and-implementation-gate`.
- The governing contract now pins the already-authoritative inbound identities:
  `malbolge-typed-ir-v1`, `malbolge-c32-v1`, `malbolge-guest-runtime-v1`,
  `malbolge_guest_runtime_bind_heap`, `malbolge_guest_intrinsic_input_word`, and
  `malbolge_guest_intrinsic_output_byte`, with host fallback explicitly
  forbidden. No ternary-stage wire identity is reserved before implementation.
- `src/compiler/ternary-lowering/` now provides a governed inbound semantic
  projection, deterministic pre-layout target model, and first fail-closed
  lowering application. The implemented slice accepts one-block no-argument
  `i32` constant-return functions, converts exact 32-bit patterns to fixed
  21-trit least-significant-first scalars, and preserves source/module
  provenance without importing typed-IR implementation types.
- `tests/ternary_lowering.rs` adapts the tracked canonical typed-IR golden only
  after complete admission, proves deterministic `return 7` lowering and exact
  source-span/identity preservation, round-trips representative extreme 32-bit
  patterns through the ternary scalar, rejects malformed/identity-drifted
  projections, and rejects a richer admitted typed-IR shape.
- The same lowering boundary now admits typed-IR successful `u8` `ByteInput` and
  `ByteOutput` effects. A valid byte-I/O fixture is admitted, canonicalized,
  restored exactly, projected, and lowered in source order; fabricated
  projections with non-`u8` input, undefined output, duplicate SSA identity, or
  byte-valued return fail closed. These target effects deliberately do not claim
  raw profile-word/EOF or declaration-only intrinsic realization.
- Remaining work includes the rest of the typed-IR operation vocabulary,
  one-shot heap startup binding, raw profile-word/EOF and exact byte-I/O
  intrinsic realization, later
  runtime helpers, target serialization, and executable Malbolge-oriented
  lowering evidence. No ternary-stage wire identity exists yet.
- Expected durable artifact surface: `compiler/`, `src/`, `tests/compiler/`.
- Required evidence: golden/round-trip or normalized stage fixtures,
  deterministic hashes where promised, and end-to-end lowering regression cases.
- Runtime realization evidence: consume guest-runtime semantic identities
  unchanged and prove their executable ternary/Malbolge lowering, including the
  one-time heap startup bind and declaration-only byte-I/O intrinsic symbols.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `typed-compiler-ir`,
  `guest-runtime-and-allocator`, `malbolge-specific-optimization-mathematics`.
